{"authored" [{"question" "q-11186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/1840ce2886aa3546371998239757a5dc500449007dc511dc0860b1ce59a59d2c.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $x=\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}+2y,$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=2,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}+2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}+2\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{8}{3}-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{44}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c6c7aa8b5a2f5b3f54cef964c69ccb34d192b68ea407470d7d558e8ecba9de6" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{22}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{350}{9}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{44}{9}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{68}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{44}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-117485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=9y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis for $y\\ge 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-117485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(9-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/bbcf218e7b6181c861ba4c804357cc53ae6004453914259a9fe98ad5f09ac4d4.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=9y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=3.$ \nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(9y-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{3}-{\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{(3)^{2}}{2}-0)-(\\frac{(3)^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}-\\frac{81}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-117485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c6c7aa8b5a2f5b3f54cef964c69ccb34d192b68ea407470d7d558e8ecba9de6" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-117485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-c