/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-117485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/446dddc9ec5393005b5aa9fff9d45760c6f2e80da97fd459cdd74cf4f8575f71.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x-1}+1,$ the $y$-axis and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{x-1}+1 \\\\ y-1 & =\\sqrt[3]{x-1} \\\\ (y-1)^{3} & =x-1 \\\\ x & =(y-1)^{3}+1 \\\\ x & ={y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}+3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+3{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}-3\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+3\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}-0)-3(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+3(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-1+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c6c7aa8b5a2f5b3f54cef964c69ccb34d192b68ea407470d7d558e8ecba9de6" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area $A$ between the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=2.$\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}} ." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x) \\\\ {e}^{y} & =3x \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{y}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{y}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,{e}^{y}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c6c7aa8b5a2f5b3f54cef964c69ccb34d192b68ea407470d7d558e8ecba9de6" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316744" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area between the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x)$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=-2$ and $y=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x) \\\\ {e}^{y} & =2-x \\\\ x & =2-{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2-{e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot y{|}_{-2}^{0}-{e}^{y}{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =2(0+2)-({e}^{0}-{e}^{-2}) \\\\  & =4-(1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/state.json" "file_sha256" "7550dae49cd5ed18e14d66479b42a1396a249b2cddb37b2fe49d1d49469adc24" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/activity-metadat