/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/0389cce819c15d700c69e6ade974bd826bb0524b355de895a27e69589ad0afd5.png)-axis, and the lines ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/81356f9909beb212c6d1c0dd7d3792dfacae911b236f1c8fa22ff0d3a508544e.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/32dbbb5be19c5504a2aa53d2f92b5df909a2417272b8c3e1d6c6f0c9f350b1d9.png) as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/example-425.json" "file_sha256" "efa73ad525176d966ea8e3d0cb3a6d25d43575a0d9c376bc1cb520aba762dde2" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/3a73881568cbe0c10ae1e24446a47a522072eb67093c9d5fd34ca0862e02be7a.png)\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/4cf2e90080f1ae459e72ac253d6617d0defdcc3be58a1ca385bddc3215034eca.png)-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/321fc255901c5f86d2c324df57b60faa428e5cbdd2cba412f643cff6df19422e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/example-425.json" "file_sha256" "efa73ad525176d966ea8e3d0cb3a6d25d43575a0d9c376bc1cb520aba762dde2" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $x=y^2-4$ and the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/example-426.json" "file_sha256" "9ea947257b3c0e18a5fbf5b6ddbc00148722703f1b9e81c52544fae02582dddf" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/f2a29faeb9db8e622a21a0e77bea911960a5c64d87a2c900ecd0c0213b2e4bce.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=y^2-4$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=-2$ to $y=2.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-8{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-8y{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-8(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-16 \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $\\left|-\\dfrac{32}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{32}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/example-426.json" "file_sha256" "9ea947257b3c0e18a5fbf5b6ddbc00148722703f1b9e81c52544fae02582dddf" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/eb7118486df97c3abae6c8492170090df0c654064799e04826a39a94bcfa22a8.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1},$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/example-6797.json" "file_sha256" "d17af83b6b1e751481a2aa58cb3a835161906ecd7b8fe240ae4f1f872217c9ad" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =x+1 \\\\ x & ={y}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}-y{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-0)-(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $\\left|-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{2}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/example-6797.json" "file_sha256" "d17af83b6b1e751481a2aa58cb3a835161906ecd7b8fe240ae4f1f872217c9ad" "basis" 1178 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area $A$ of the closed region between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis for $y\\le 0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/state.json" "file_sha256" "a902c7092c09348011210bf90daa61e6b2c9f0c8414432d41a9efc6546e99132" "basis" 1219 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{4}-16) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{2}-4)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y(y-2)(y+2)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/assets/03737836a352eafaf486e7e5f71d882ac39715e788a0c9113eb809b185584bdc.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-2$ to $y=0.$\nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{y}^{6}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}(0-(-64))-\\frac{3}{2}(0-4) \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/state.json" "file_sha256" "a902c7092c09348011210bf90daa61e6b2c9f0c8414432d41a9efc6546e99132" "basis" 1219 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "59fb94a788f53441d81416cbfaf34fc8b55d68af210510bf04f352110862cd72" "basis" 1219 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346674" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/state.json" "file_sha256" "a902c7092c09348011210bf90daa61e6b2c9f0c8414432d41a9efc6546e99132" "basis" 1219 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346674" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/state.json" "file_sha256" "a902c7092c09348011210bf90daa61e6b2c9f0c8414432d41a9efc6546e99132" "basis" 1219 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-346401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/94ef52e454545335132d467773c0b274296a7cb3758ae9fae3242876c8063f5f.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{2}-3y$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=2$ and $y=4,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-346401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}(\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{2}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,-\\,3{\\int }_{2}^{4}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{2}^{4}\\,-\\,3\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(\\frac{64}{3}-\\frac{8}{3})\\,-\\,3(8-2) \\\\  & =14-18 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $|-4|=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-346401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-346401" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-346401" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area bounded between the curve $x=-4{y}^{2}+12,$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-4{y}^{2}+12)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+12{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-4\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+12\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+12(1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}+12 \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-11301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{12}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{22}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{40}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{32}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11183" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/96a2d22126a8f2575ae97bae8e4a20ef6e7a99fc888b2ce7102c731963d63fea.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $x={y}^{2}+2y,$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=-2,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11183" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}({y}^{2}+2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+2{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{-2}^{0}+2\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3})+2(0-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $|-\\frac{4}{3}|=\\frac{4}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11183" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-11183" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11183" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{11}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11183" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-346428" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/25f1ddf290a96f1ef7393d33583b2f519bf8b5c8e66166240345a611d10fba96.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded between the curve $x=5{y}^{4}+3$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-346428" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(5{y}^{4}+3)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y+3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={y}^{5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+3y\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =({1}^{5}-{0}^{5})+3(1-0) \\\\  & =1+3 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-346428" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-346428" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-346428" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/1840ce2886aa3546371998239757a5dc500449007dc511dc0860b1ce59a59d2c.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $x=\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}+2y,$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=2,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}+2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}+2\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{8}{3}-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{44}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "\\frac{22}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{350}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{44}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{68}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-11186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{44}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $x={y}^{3}-6{y}^{2}+9y$ and the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}-6{y}^{2}+9y & =0 \\\\ y({y}^{2}-6y+9) & =0 \\\\ y(y-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/7509bf6a10838458b110d982740c1399aa36279b9ce4a231f99b76d7c7cee0b3.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x={y}^{3}-6{y}^{2}+9y$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=3.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}({y}^{3}-6{y}^{2}+9y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y-6{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+9{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{3}-6\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{3}+9\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{3}^{4}}{4}-0)-6(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}-0)+9(\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}-54+\\frac{81}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-117487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "9"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{27}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=9y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis for $y\\ge 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(9-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/bbcf218e7b6181c861ba4c804357cc53ae6004453914259a9fe98ad5f09ac4d4.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=9y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=3.$ \nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(9y-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{3}-{\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{(3)^{2}}{2}-0)-(\\frac{(3)^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}-\\frac{81}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-117485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "27"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{81}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{81}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{81}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-346674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area $A$ of the closed region between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis for $y\\le 0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-346674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{4}-16) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{2}-4)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y(y-2)(y+2)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/03737836a352eafaf486e7e5f71d882ac39715e788a0c9113eb809b185584bdc.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-2$ to $y=0.$\nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{y}^{6}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}(0-(-64))-\\frac{3}{2}(0-4) \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-346674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-346674" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-346674" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area $A$ of the finite region bounded between the curve $x={y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}+25y$ and the $y$-axis. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}+25y & =0 \\\\ y({y}^{2}-10y+25) & =0 \\\\ y(y-5)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/593d1168ce7328aa93edd61fcabc116451fcda8ef24faeac0949fa0a8e686b51.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x={y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}+25y$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=5.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}\\,({y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}+25y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y-10{\\int }_{0}^{5}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+25{\\int }_{0}^{5}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}|}_{0}^{5}-{\\frac{10}{3}{y}^{3}|}_{0}^{5}+{\\frac{25}{2}{y}^{2}|}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{5}^{4}}{4}-0)-\\frac{10}{3}({5}^{3}-0)+\\frac{25}{2}({5}^{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{625}{4}-\\frac{1250}{3}+\\frac{625}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{625}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-316714" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316714" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{625}{12}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-10031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/b77e20a705956f80379158fd88de70f95c94989c6bd7640d1f3c20d8cca7b4f5.png)\n\nFind the area of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis, as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-10031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(1-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that we want to find the area between the curve $x=y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis from $y=0$ to $y=1.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1}-{\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}-0)-(\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-10031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-10031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-10031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-10031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-78900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area between the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x)$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=-2$ and $y=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-78900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x) \\\\ {e}^{y} & =2-x \\\\ x & =2-{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2-{e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot y{|}_{-2}^{0}-{e}^{y}{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =2(0+2)-({e}^{0}-{e}^{-2}) \\\\  & =4-(1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-78900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-78900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-78900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}"] ["math" "1+e"] ["math" "3+\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}"] ["math" "3+{e}^{2}"] ["math" "5+e"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-78900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3+\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/a988c243bcf4b82cd05b1ed0292e0595141dbe37a470abc34b183f0ce184fe3f.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x+8}-2$, the $y$-axis and the lines $y=-2$ and $y=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{x+8}-2 \\\\ y+2 & =\\sqrt[3]{x+8} \\\\ (y+2)^{3} & =x+8 \\\\ x & =(y+2)^{3}-8 \\\\ x & ={y}^{3}+6{y}^{2}+12y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}({y}^{3}+6{y}^{2}+12y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{-2}^{0}\\,+\\,6\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{-2}^{0}+12\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-\\frac{16}{4})+6(0-(-\\frac{8}{3}))+12(0-\\frac{4}{2}) \\\\  & =-4+16-24 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is\n\n$$\nA=|-12|=12\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-316742" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316742" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area $A$ between the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=2.$\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}} ." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x) \\\\ {e}^{y} & =3x \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{y}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{y}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,{e}^{y}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-316744" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-316744" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{e^2-1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/446dddc9ec5393005b5aa9fff9d45760c6f2e80da97fd459cdd74cf4f8575f71.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x-1}+1,$ the $y$-axis and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{x-1}+1 \\\\ y-1 & =\\sqrt[3]{x-1} \\\\ (y-1)^{3} & =x-1 \\\\ x & =(y-1)^{3}+1 \\\\ x & ={y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}+3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+3{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}-3\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+3\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}-0)-3(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+3(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-1+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-78896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})$, the $y$-axis, and lines  $y=1$ and $y=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}) \\\\ {e}^{y} & =\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ x & =2{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{e}^{y}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =2({e}^{3}-{e}^{1}) \\\\  & =2({e}^{3}-e)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5c9414e867e46e7a978eadd73fe6d018f4a8359ce631ef9da40b3fda734123f"} {"question" "q-117637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2({e}^{3}-1)"] ["math" "2({e}^{3}-e)"] ["math" "2{e}^{3}-e"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{3}-e}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "q-117637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2({e}^{3}-e)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/state.json" "file_sha256" "c446d9d0e6232f2cfd22ad1245543d5acfdfb747eee28c14e26fb1c27bde59bc"} {"question" "e-425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/bf61fd6b36dd17d2c9f6d6f570a8bad9111d10da11df8f69e39069d7fb4478cf.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/8cdef67ff9afa667ed298cc0bb29e1727cfd7208fca347fb2b0ae253a1abdebf.png) the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/0389cce819c15d700c69e6ade974bd826bb0524b355de895a27e69589ad0afd5.png)-axis, and the lines ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/81356f9909beb212c6d1c0dd7d3792dfacae911b236f1c8fa22ff0d3a508544e.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/32dbbb5be19c5504a2aa53d2f92b5df909a2417272b8c3e1d6c6f0c9f350b1d9.png) as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/example-425.json" "file_sha256" "23c256b0667b4e4f16c11d1de29399f97a1162f55d95f6c4c709b78666235075"} {"question" "e-425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/3a73881568cbe0c10ae1e24446a47a522072eb67093c9d5fd34ca0862e02be7a.png)\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/4cf2e90080f1ae459e72ac253d6617d0defdcc3be58a1ca385bddc3215034eca.png)-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/321fc255901c5f86d2c324df57b60faa428e5cbdd2cba412f643cff6df19422e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/example-425.json" "file_sha256" "23c256b0667b4e4f16c11d1de29399f97a1162f55d95f6c4c709b78666235075"} {"question" "e-426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $x=y^2-4$ and the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/example-426.json" "file_sha256" "9be8cf9935a03ff54803511f2ff21a78dbace8b8c0ddfb318a2b3fc9535a2f08"} {"question" "e-426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/f2a29faeb9db8e622a21a0e77bea911960a5c64d87a2c900ecd0c0213b2e4bce.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=y^2-4$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=-2$ to $y=2.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-8{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-8y{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-8(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-16 \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $\\left|-\\dfrac{32}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{32}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/example-426.json" "file_sha256" "9be8cf9935a03ff54803511f2ff21a78dbace8b8c0ddfb318a2b3fc9535a2f08"} {"question" "e-6797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/assets/eb7118486df97c3abae6c8492170090df0c654064799e04826a39a94bcfa22a8.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1},$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/example-6797.json" "file_sha256" "cd8b76f625a9dde2476d3904919ac385fa41b58e228aa640c73e18fd59ab951e"} {"question" "e-6797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =x+1 \\\\ x & ={y}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}-y{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-0)-(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $\\left|-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{2}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082348/example-6797.json" "file_sha256" "cd8b76f625a9dde2476d3904919ac385fa41b58e228aa640c73e18fd59ab951e"}] "usage" {"q-346674" [] "e-426" [] "q-316744" [] "e-6797" [] "q-78896" [] "e-425" [] "q-117485" [] "q-78900" [] "q-11186" []} "basis" 2853 "retractions" [[17592186291643 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/1840ce2886aa3546371998239757a5dc500449007dc511dc0860b1ce59a59d2c.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $x=\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}+2y,$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=2,$ as shown above."] [17592186291657 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(9-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/bbcf218e7b6181c861ba4c804357cc53ae6004453914259a9fe98ad5f09ac4d4.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=9y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=3.$ \nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(9y-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{3}-{\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{(3)^{2}}{2}-0)-(\\frac{(3)^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}-\\frac{81}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186293424 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{4}-16) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y({y}^{2}-4)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{16}y(y-2)(y+2)({y}^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032052/assets/03737836a352eafaf486e7e5f71d882ac39715e788a0c9113eb809b185584bdc.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-2$ to $y=0.$\nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{5}-3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{y}^{6}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}(0-(-64))-\\frac{3}{2}(0-4) \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186291698 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/446dddc9ec5393005b5aa9fff9d45760c6f2e80da97fd459cdd74cf4f8575f71.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x-1}+1,$ the $y$-axis and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above."] [17592186096358 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/bf61fd6b36dd17d2c9f6d6f570a8bad9111d10da11df8f69e39069d7fb4478cf.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/8cdef67ff9afa667ed298cc0bb29e1727cfd7208fca347fb2b0ae253a1abdebf.png) the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/0389cce819c15d700c69e6ade974bd826bb0524b355de895a27e69589ad0afd5.png)-axis, and the lines ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/81356f9909beb212c6d1c0dd7d3792dfacae911b236f1c8fa22ff0d3a508544e.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/32dbbb5be19c5504a2aa53d2